1
00:04:11,428 --> 00:04:17,428
Meet the Patels is a romance, comedy, documentary film directed by Ravi Patel.

2
00:08:22,857 --> 00:08:28,857
Finding love is never easy.

3
00:12:34,285 --> 00:12:40,285
For Ravi Patel, a first generation Indian-American, the odds are slim.

4
00:16:45,714 --> 00:16:51,714
His ideal bride is beautiful, smart, funny, family-oriented, kind and—in
keeping with tradition—Indian (though hopefully raised in the US).

5
00:20:57,142 --> 00:21:03,142
Oh, and her last name should be Patel because in
India, Patels usually marry other Patels.

6
00:25:08,571 --> 00:25:14,571
And so at 30, Ravi decides to break up with his American girlfriend (the one who by all accounts is perfect for him except
for her red hair and American name) and embark on a worldwide search for another Patel longing to be loved.

7
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:26,000
He enlists the help of his matchmaker mother, attends a convention of
Patels living in the US and travels to wedding season in India.

8
00:33:31,428 --> 00:33:37,428
Witty, honest and heartfelt, this comedy explores the
questions with which we all struggle: What is love?

9
00:37:42,857 --> 00:37:48,857
What is happiness?

10
00:41:54,285 --> 00:42:00,285
And how in the world do we go about finding them?

11
00:46:05,714 --> 00:46:11,714
Self, played by Ravi Patel.

12
00:50:17,142 --> 00:50:23,142
Self, played by Geeta Patel.

13
00:54:28,571 --> 00:54:34,571
Self, played by Champa V. Patel.

14
00:58:40,000 --> 00:58:46,000
Self, played by Vasant K. Patel.

15
01:02:51,428 --> 01:02:57,428
Self, played by Audrey Wauchope.

16
01:07:02,857 --> 01:07:08,857
Meet the Patels is a 2014 American romantic comedy documentary film
directed by siblings Geeta Patel and Ravi Patel.

17
01:11:14,285 --> 01:11:20,285
The film explores the expectations surrounding marriage in the Patels'
first-generation Indian immigrant family and in wider American society.

18
01:15:25,714 --> 01:15:31,714
It had its international premiere at Hot Docs in April 2014.

19
01:19:37,142 --> 01:19:43,142
Fox Searchlight acquired remake rights after the documentary won
the Audience Award at the Los Angeles Film Festival.

20
01:23:48,571 --> 01:23:54,571
The tone is lighthearted and uplifting and emotional.
